WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:05.046 --> 00:00:06.881
In the not-so-distant future,

00:00:06.881 --> 00:00:09.676
the world is going to be
a very different place.

00:00:11.553 --> 00:00:14.264
China is becoming the
world's biggest economy.

00:00:14.264 --> 00:00:17.726
We would expect China to
overtake the United States

00:00:17.726 --> 00:00:19.811
pretty quickly, perhaps around

00:00:19.811 --> 00:00:22.814
the turn of the decade in 2030.

00:00:22.814 --> 00:00:26.317
Its share of global
trade actually increased

00:00:26.317 --> 00:00:28.111
at a record clip.

00:00:28.111 --> 00:00:30.155
China's meteoric economic rise

00:00:30.155 --> 00:00:32.365
is unprecedented in history.

00:00:32.365 --> 00:00:34.367
There's something called China time,

00:00:34.367 --> 00:00:36.369
where everything happens so much faster.

00:00:39.247 --> 00:00:41.750
The reality of the last 40 years

00:00:41.750 --> 00:00:45.920
has been a radical shift
from agrarian poverty

00:00:45.920 --> 00:00:48.048
at the end of the Mao era

00:00:48.048 --> 00:00:49.966
to something which looks like

00:00:49.966 --> 00:00:52.427
a comfortable, middle class life.

00:00:53.720 --> 00:00:56.598
Opening up to market
capitalism in the late 70's

00:00:56.598 --> 00:00:58.433
kick-started a new era.

00:00:59.642 --> 00:01:01.519
The trappings of Western capitalism

00:01:01.519 --> 00:01:03.897
are now ubiquitous in China,

00:01:03.897 --> 00:01:06.608
but so too is the iron fist of the state.

00:01:07.901 --> 00:01:10.070
While it undoubtedly comes at a cost,

00:01:10.070 --> 00:01:12.363
this central control has allowed Beijing

00:01:12.363 --> 00:01:15.533
to nurture long-term economic strategies.

00:01:15.533 --> 00:01:17.285
China has transformed itself into

00:01:17.285 --> 00:01:19.370
a green energy powerhouse that produces

00:01:19.370 --> 00:01:22.540
most of the world's solar
panels, wind turbines

00:01:22.540 --> 00:01:24.125
and lithium-ion batteries.

00:01:25.210 --> 00:01:27.879
By 2030, China is poised to grab

00:01:27.879 --> 00:01:29.631
the lion's share of jobs and wealth

00:01:29.631 --> 00:01:33.259
as the world gradually transitions
away from fossil fuels

00:01:35.178 --> 00:01:38.765
and it's become fertile ground
for electric car makers.

00:01:38.765 --> 00:01:41.226
At GM, we believe China will be

00:01:41.226 --> 00:01:43.853
one of the main epicenters in the globe

00:01:43.853 --> 00:01:45.772
of the adoption or the transformation

00:01:45.772 --> 00:01:49.400
towards the electrification of the vehicle.

00:01:49.400 --> 00:01:52.987
China is rewriting the
rules of global capitalism.

00:01:52.987 --> 00:01:55.448
Can the rest of the world keep up?

00:01:55.448 --> 00:01:57.200
You know, the President is concerned

00:01:57.200 --> 00:01:59.536
that China is far ahead of us.

00:01:59.536 --> 00:02:01.454
It is time for that to shift around.

00:02:12.173 --> 00:02:13.466
While China has become a leader

00:02:13.466 --> 00:02:15.385
in multiple green industries,

00:02:15.385 --> 00:02:17.595
the progress it has made
in electric vehicles

00:02:17.595 --> 00:02:20.014
or EVs is unparalleled.

00:02:21.266 --> 00:02:23.852
The evolution of the
automobile in the 20th century

00:02:23.852 --> 00:02:27.438
caused an economic revolution
in the United States.

00:02:27.438 --> 00:02:30.650
After losing out to international
carmakers for decades,

00:02:30.650 --> 00:02:34.654
China has learned to leapfrog
the combustion engine.

00:02:34.654 --> 00:02:36.573
The country is already
home to the planet's

00:02:36.573 --> 00:02:39.367
largest market for EVs by sales,

00:02:39.367 --> 00:02:40.869
and it still has room to grow.

00:02:41.953 --> 00:02:45.165
Electric cars account
for 5% of sales today,

00:02:45.165 --> 00:02:49.544
but Beijing is aiming for that
figure to hit 40% by 2030.

00:02:52.130 --> 00:02:56.176
Back in 2001, Beijing drew
up the 863 initiative

00:02:56.176 --> 00:02:58.261
to strengthen the competitiveness of China

00:02:58.261 --> 00:02:59.554
in the global economy.

00:03:00.597 --> 00:03:03.099
It invested a relatively small amount,

00:03:03.099 --> 00:03:05.935
about $130 million into three

00:03:05.935 --> 00:03:08.479
new energy vehicle technologies,

00:03:08.479 --> 00:03:11.191
fuel cell, hybrid and electric.

00:03:12.233 --> 00:03:14.819
These guided China's
green vehicle development

00:03:14.819 --> 00:03:16.779
for the next 15 years.

00:03:16.779 --> 00:03:21.075
There is a technology
race on renewable energy

00:03:21.075 --> 00:03:22.827
and electric cars that's emerging

00:03:22.827 --> 00:03:25.038
between the United States and China.

00:03:25.038 --> 00:03:28.499
Right now, China is ahead on electric cars

00:03:28.499 --> 00:03:31.336
because the government has
had a very strong policy

00:03:31.336 --> 00:03:34.839
supporting electric cars
now for a number of years.

00:03:34.839 --> 00:03:37.050
I've been going to
China for about 25 years

00:03:37.050 --> 00:03:39.802
and the changes are just amazing.

00:03:39.802 --> 00:03:42.639
When I first went to China,
the streets were filled

00:03:42.639 --> 00:03:46.476
with swarms, swarms and
swarms of bicyclists,

00:03:46.476 --> 00:03:49.103
almost in this graceful swimming thing

00:03:49.103 --> 00:03:51.022
as people were bicycling to work.

00:03:51.022 --> 00:03:53.566
All gone, just streets now jammed

00:03:53.566 --> 00:03:55.735
and you can sit there in
the longest traffic jams

00:03:55.735 --> 00:03:59.864
I've ever been in and
that's just one 

00:03:59.864 --> 00:04:01.032
sign of the change.

00:04:01.950 --> 00:04:03.993
They realize that
there's one global market

00:04:03.993 --> 00:04:05.495
where they cannot be competitive.

00:04:05.495 --> 00:04:07.163
They're too late, the traditional

00:04:07.163 --> 00:04:09.916
gasoline, petrol-powered car,

00:04:09.916 --> 00:04:11.542
but they see themselves, if they can get

00:04:11.542 --> 00:04:13.795
at the forefront on electric vehicles

00:04:13.795 --> 00:04:15.838
and almost half the world's electric cars

00:04:15.838 --> 00:04:17.715
now are in China, that will give them

00:04:17.715 --> 00:04:20.218
a foundation to be very strong competitors

00:04:20.218 --> 00:04:22.762
in the global automobile
market of the future,

00:04:22.762 --> 00:04:24.305
which they are not now.

00:04:26.641 --> 00:04:28.559
This technological leapfrogging means

00:04:28.559 --> 00:04:30.603
many of us haven't seen or even heard of

00:04:30.603 --> 00:04:33.648
some of China's biggest automakers.

00:04:44.867 --> 00:04:47.203
Like so many other Chinese companies,

00:04:47.203 --> 00:04:48.663
Geely had grown into a behemoth

00:04:48.663 --> 00:04:51.749
long before it started to operate abroad.

00:04:51.749 --> 00:04:55.211
Now, it owns Volvo,
has a stake in Daimler,

00:04:55.211 --> 00:04:56.713
and is listed internationally.

00:04:57.797 --> 00:05:00.675
Geely isn't selling as many
cars as Tesla just yet,

00:05:00.675 --> 00:05:03.177
but it is able to launch bold new concepts

00:05:03.177 --> 00:05:06.097
in an environment that
actively encourages innovation,

00:05:06.097 --> 00:05:09.058
such as its new rapid
battery-swap stations.

00:05:24.490 --> 00:05:26.492
This is a technology Tesla didn't think

00:05:26.492 --> 00:05:28.870
Western countries were ready for.

00:05:28.870 --> 00:05:30.496
It's amazing, if you go back two decades,

00:05:30.496 --> 00:05:33.082
China was a tiny automobile market,

00:05:33.082 --> 00:05:34.751
one or two million cars a year.

00:05:34.751 --> 00:05:37.670
Now it's like 27 million cars a year,

00:05:37.670 --> 00:05:40.548
which is like 50% bigger
than the U.S. market.

00:05:40.548 --> 00:05:43.634
So, that gives them a test bed

00:05:43.634 --> 00:05:45.386
for promoting electric cars,

00:05:45.386 --> 00:05:47.096
which they're doing aggressively.

00:05:47.096 --> 00:05:50.058
It also means that the
automobile makers of the world,

00:05:50.058 --> 00:05:51.434
and remember, the automobile business

00:05:51.434 --> 00:05:53.436
is a global business, they may be

00:05:53.436 --> 00:05:55.605
focused on the United
States, but they also

00:05:55.605 --> 00:05:58.775
wanna sell electric cars
and be competitive in China.

00:06:02.695 --> 00:06:04.489
China's vast domestic market,

00:06:04.489 --> 00:06:07.492
400 million middle-class car buyers

00:06:07.492 --> 00:06:09.535
means that major international carmakers

00:06:09.535 --> 00:06:11.704
have to invest and compete there.

00:06:14.665 --> 00:06:16.834
Beijing may be able to
take advantage of that

00:06:16.834 --> 00:06:18.836
to further its strategic ambition

00:06:18.836 --> 00:06:20.421
of clean-tech dominance,

00:06:20.421 --> 00:06:22.090
but that's not to say it's a hard sell

00:06:22.090 --> 00:06:23.633
for foreign car companies.

00:06:25.343 --> 00:06:28.471
The city of Liuzhou,
thanks to a green push

00:06:28.471 --> 00:06:31.140
by local authorities
has effectively become

00:06:31.140 --> 00:06:34.435
the capital of the biggest
EV market in the world.

00:06:34.435 --> 00:06:38.606
They basically have
created lanes in the city

00:06:38.606 --> 00:06:40.274
where electric cars can go,

00:06:40.274 --> 00:06:43.319
and, like, normal
combustion engines can't.

00:06:43.319 --> 00:06:45.321
And the majority of these electric cars

00:06:45.321 --> 00:06:49.117
are three meters long,
cost less than $5,000,

00:06:49.117 --> 00:06:50.660
and out-sell Teslas.

00:06:50.660 --> 00:06:53.371
They've created dedicated parking spaces

00:06:53.371 --> 00:06:55.456
that are half the size
of normal parking spaces

00:06:55.456 --> 00:06:56.999
that can only be used by those.

00:06:56.999 --> 00:06:59.669
So, you've created an environment where

00:06:59.669 --> 00:07:01.254
it's an advantage in that city

00:07:01.254 --> 00:07:02.880
to have a Hong Guang mini EV.

00:07:02.880 --> 00:07:06.092
So, it's a positive example of how to

00:07:06.092 --> 00:07:08.845
encourage usage of products

00:07:08.845 --> 00:07:12.306
that helps drive consumer behavior.

00:07:12.306 --> 00:07:15.184
The cars are made by a
Chinese company called Wuling

00:07:15.184 --> 00:07:16.269
in partnership with a

00:07:16.269 --> 00:07:19.605
very famous American
company, General Motors.

00:07:19.605 --> 00:07:22.859
♪ Baseball, hotdogs,
apple pie and Chevrolet ♪

00:07:22.859 --> 00:07:26.446
♪ They go together in the good old USA ♪

00:07:26.446 --> 00:07:30.116
♪ Baseball, hotdogs,
apple pie and Chevrolet ♪

00:07:30.116 --> 00:07:32.869
Once a symbol of American
industrial might,

00:07:32.869 --> 00:07:34.495
General Motors has to now look

00:07:34.495 --> 00:07:37.498
outside the U.S. for opportunity.

00:07:37.498 --> 00:07:40.209
China has become the
company's biggest market

00:07:40.209 --> 00:07:43.296
and is, by far, the most
strategically important.

00:07:43.296 --> 00:07:45.715
The Chinese consumer is very tech savvy.

00:07:45.715 --> 00:07:48.009
This means you've got
a very fertile ground

00:07:48.009 --> 00:07:50.720
to try new things, to experiment

00:07:50.720 --> 00:07:53.473
and to get people to adopt new technology.

00:07:53.473 --> 00:07:55.224
Every car we make we sell,

00:07:55.224 --> 00:07:56.934
and this is not regulation-driven,

00:07:56.934 --> 00:07:58.644
this is pure customer demand

00:07:58.644 --> 00:08:00.771
that is driving the need for us

00:08:00.771 --> 00:08:02.773
to supply that product to consumers.

00:08:02.773 --> 00:08:05.610
In China, electric car
buyers can get subsidies

00:08:05.610 --> 00:08:07.778
worth thousands of dollars.

00:08:07.778 --> 00:08:10.031
In some cities, getting a parking permit

00:08:10.031 --> 00:08:12.450
for a conventional combustion engine car

00:08:12.450 --> 00:08:14.035
has become nearly impossible.

00:08:14.827 --> 00:08:17.038
At the end of 2020, the country had

00:08:17.038 --> 00:08:20.958
1.68 million charging points for EVs.

00:08:20.958 --> 00:08:25.796
Compare that with 72,000 in
the U.S. at the end of 2019.

00:08:25.796 --> 00:08:28.257
The vast majority of
Chinese driving habits

00:08:28.257 --> 00:08:31.219
and actual miles driven
or kilometers driven

00:08:31.219 --> 00:08:32.970
is in an urban environment,
which obviously

00:08:32.970 --> 00:08:37.016
suits the adoption of electric vehicles.

00:08:37.016 --> 00:08:38.768
If you look at the Hong Guang Mini EV,

00:08:38.768 --> 00:08:42.980
we have ranges of 170
kilometers and 120 kilometers,

00:08:42.980 --> 00:08:45.733
but for the vast majority
of our consumers that,

00:08:45.733 --> 00:08:47.693
it's either a second car
or it's a primary car

00:08:47.693 --> 00:08:49.987
in a real downtown area, that's adequate

00:08:49.987 --> 00:08:51.072
because of driving conditions

00:08:51.072 --> 00:08:52.532
and the charging infrastructure mean

00:08:52.532 --> 00:08:54.617
that you've got a very high adoption rate

00:08:54.617 --> 00:08:56.911
and not so many barriers to adoption.

00:08:57.578 --> 00:08:58.871
There's a clear tipping point

00:08:58.871 --> 00:09:02.166
around the 250, 300 mile mark in the U.S.

00:09:02.166 --> 00:09:04.544
That is because a lot
of consumers in the U.S.

00:09:04.544 --> 00:09:06.754
drive, you know, city to city.

00:09:06.754 --> 00:09:09.131
So that's a big part of life.

00:09:09.131 --> 00:09:10.424
That's a little different in China.

00:09:10.424 --> 00:09:14.387
85% of miles driven are driven
in a non-highway environment.

00:09:15.429 --> 00:09:19.183
The Chinese aren't just
transforming the EV market.

00:09:19.183 --> 00:09:21.102
A government-led, top-down approach

00:09:21.102 --> 00:09:23.854
also rewrites the rules of innovation.

00:09:25.106 --> 00:09:28.651
In the Western conception,
the entrepreneur

00:09:28.651 --> 00:09:32.822
is critical in the innovation process.

00:09:32.822 --> 00:09:35.700
It's the entrepreneur, the Bill Gates,

00:09:35.700 --> 00:09:39.161
the Jeff Bezos, and
the financial incentive

00:09:39.161 --> 00:09:42.707
that innovation will
deliver enormous wealth

00:09:42.707 --> 00:09:46.877
that's the catalyst for
the innovation process.

00:09:46.877 --> 00:09:49.463
That's part of the picture,

00:09:49.463 --> 00:09:51.549
but as we're discovering in China,

00:09:51.549 --> 00:09:53.926
it's not the entire picture.

00:09:53.926 --> 00:09:56.596
A government which is willing to patiently

00:09:56.596 --> 00:10:01.517
pour resources, time, money, people

00:10:01.517 --> 00:10:05.229
into solving problems and
pushing innovation forward

00:10:05.229 --> 00:10:08.274
can also deliver some impressive results.

00:10:09.775 --> 00:10:12.653
The majority of the cars GM sells in China

00:10:12.653 --> 00:10:15.156
are made in China, which means the company

00:10:15.156 --> 00:10:18.909
has to walk on eggshells to
stay in Beijing's good graces.

00:10:18.909 --> 00:10:21.245
It represents the dilemma
most foreign companies

00:10:21.245 --> 00:10:23.539
face in the country.

00:10:23.539 --> 00:10:27.043
To catch up in clean-tech,
there's a trade-off...

00:10:27.043 --> 00:10:29.545
My name is Joe Biden and I'm a car guy.

00:10:29.545 --> 00:10:32.340
Which is why investment
in EV charging stations

00:10:32.340 --> 00:10:34.091
is part of President Biden's new

00:10:34.091 --> 00:10:36.886
$1.2 trillion infrastructure plan.

00:10:36.886 --> 00:10:39.221
You know, the President is concerned

00:10:39.221 --> 00:10:41.015
that China is far ahead of us

00:10:41.015 --> 00:10:42.642
in the electric vehicle market,

00:10:42.642 --> 00:10:46.020
and instead of producing the
technologies of the future,

00:10:46.020 --> 00:10:48.522
we are importing them from somewhere else.

00:10:48.522 --> 00:10:51.025
It is time for that to shift around.

00:10:51.025 --> 00:10:53.986
Not everyone on Biden's
team is alarmed though.

00:10:53.986 --> 00:10:57.782
I would venture to guess
that the vast majority

00:10:57.782 --> 00:11:01.243
of all patents and innovations

00:11:01.243 --> 00:11:03.287
in the clean tech space has been funded

00:11:03.287 --> 00:11:05.373
by the Department of Energy and by

00:11:05.373 --> 00:11:08.042
private sector players
within the United States.

00:11:08.042 --> 00:11:10.169
They were commercialized
largely, I would say,

00:11:10.169 --> 00:11:12.171
in Europe through the
Feed-in Tariff programs

00:11:12.171 --> 00:11:15.841
and in China, through their
manufacturing prowess,

00:11:15.841 --> 00:11:18.761
but a lot of the technology
really originated

00:11:18.761 --> 00:11:20.721
here in the United States

00:11:20.721 --> 00:11:22.181
but I think if you were to think about

00:11:22.181 --> 00:11:25.017
what the most innovative
electric vehicles are

00:11:25.017 --> 00:11:27.311
in the world, you'd think of Tesla,

00:11:27.311 --> 00:11:28.396
and I think when you think about

00:11:28.396 --> 00:11:31.732
who all of the players,
including the Chinese players,

00:11:31.732 --> 00:11:34.360
want to emulate, it's American innovation.

00:11:34.360 --> 00:11:35.986
It's not Chinese innovation.

00:11:37.905 --> 00:11:40.282
The current lithium-ion battery technology,

00:11:40.282 --> 00:11:43.327
really no one believes that
that current technology

00:11:43.327 --> 00:11:45.329
will be relevant in 2030.

00:11:45.329 --> 00:11:47.331
Whether it's the cathode or the anode

00:11:47.331 --> 00:11:49.625
or the electrolyte or the substrates,

00:11:49.625 --> 00:11:53.796
I think everyone sees a
dramatic amount of innovation

00:11:53.796 --> 00:11:55.673
in the next generation of battery storage,

00:11:55.673 --> 00:11:58.509
which is what we're scaling
up here in the United States.

00:12:01.721 --> 00:12:04.348
There are facets to China's
success in clean tech

00:12:04.348 --> 00:12:06.976
that are problematic to say the least.

00:12:06.976 --> 00:12:09.186
Its booming solar
industry has been accused

00:12:09.186 --> 00:12:12.106
of relying, to some
degree, on forced labor.

00:12:12.106 --> 00:12:14.400
Where systemic oppression
of Muslim Uyghurs

00:12:14.400 --> 00:12:17.528
is an international human rights issue.

00:12:17.528 --> 00:12:20.156
Justice! Give us our justice!

00:12:20.156 --> 00:12:21.949
China is also the world's biggest

00:12:21.949 --> 00:12:23.993
greenhouse gas emitter, and is home

00:12:23.993 --> 00:12:25.911
to huge environmental problems,

00:12:25.911 --> 00:12:28.247
mainly thanks to its reluctance to rein in

00:12:28.247 --> 00:12:29.457
its massive coal industry.

00:12:31.083 --> 00:12:33.711
When severe air pollution
swept across the country

00:12:33.711 --> 00:12:36.797
in the winter of 2013,
Beijing tilted further

00:12:36.797 --> 00:12:38.632
towards green car policies.

00:12:39.675 --> 00:12:42.970
Over the past 30 days, the average

00:12:42.970 --> 00:12:45.222
air quality level in this city

00:12:45.222 --> 00:12:48.726
has registered as hazardous
on the official scale.

00:12:49.769 --> 00:12:52.021
By 2019, the government had designed

00:12:52.021 --> 00:12:55.024
a world-beating system
of regulatory targets

00:12:55.024 --> 00:12:56.525
which has required automakers

00:12:56.525 --> 00:12:58.486
to accelerate investment in sales

00:12:58.486 --> 00:13:00.696
of electric cars faster
than they might have

00:13:00.696 --> 00:13:03.115
left to their own devices.

00:13:03.115 --> 00:13:06.410
All this has set China on course for 2030,

00:13:06.410 --> 00:13:08.788
where the country will
have an out-sized influence

00:13:08.788 --> 00:13:11.207
in this strategic industry, with a big say

00:13:11.207 --> 00:13:14.418
over technical standards
and terms of trade.

00:13:14.418 --> 00:13:16.879
The big question, the Chinese,

00:13:16.879 --> 00:13:19.757
state-sponsored conception of capitalism

00:13:19.757 --> 00:13:23.469
worked really well when
China was catching up,

00:13:23.469 --> 00:13:25.888
borrowing from, or some would say,

00:13:25.888 --> 00:13:29.767
stealing technologies from
the rest of the world.

00:13:29.767 --> 00:13:32.645
Will it work so well
when China has reached

00:13:32.645 --> 00:13:34.814
the technology frontier and needs

00:13:34.814 --> 00:13:36.565
to innovate through it?

00:13:36.565 --> 00:13:38.901
I think you could have two scenarios.

00:13:38.901 --> 00:13:41.695
One is, it actually
doesn't look too different,

00:13:41.695 --> 00:13:43.697
a lot more electric cars on the road,

00:13:43.697 --> 00:13:46.909
traffic still a really big problem.

00:13:46.909 --> 00:13:50.496
The other is, what I
describe in 'The New Map'

00:13:50.496 --> 00:13:53.290
as auto tech, where
you take electric cars,

00:13:53.290 --> 00:13:54.667
put it together with ride-hailing,

00:13:54.667 --> 00:13:57.378
put it together with
self-driving, autonomous vehicles,

00:13:57.378 --> 00:14:00.756
and you have these very
large fleets of cars,

00:14:00.756 --> 00:14:01.924
self-driving, that just come

00:14:01.924 --> 00:14:03.926
and pick people up and people don't really

00:14:03.926 --> 00:14:05.386
identify with their car anymore.

00:14:05.386 --> 00:14:07.263
It's just a utility of facility,

00:14:07.263 --> 00:14:10.432
and it's kind of moving
in a very different way,

00:14:10.432 --> 00:14:12.226
and you don't have traffic jams

00:14:12.226 --> 00:14:14.603
because everybody is well coordinated.

00:14:14.603 --> 00:14:16.856
So, it's all these vehicles are

00:14:16.856 --> 00:14:18.691
tied together by software.

00:14:18.691 --> 00:14:21.443
So, I think it's not a
prediction of one or the other,

00:14:21.443 --> 00:14:23.529
but rather two scenarios.

00:14:23.529 --> 00:14:26.574
A lot depends upon the pace of technology,

00:14:26.574 --> 00:14:28.701
and I think a lot depends upon

00:14:28.701 --> 00:14:32.496
how this competition and
interdependence at the same time

00:14:32.496 --> 00:14:35.207
between China and the
United States plays out.

00:14:36.625 --> 00:14:39.378
Cutting edge EVs rely on a lot of software

00:14:39.378 --> 00:14:42.464
and data for onboard navigation, charging,

00:14:42.464 --> 00:14:45.759
wireless updates, and remote diagnostics.

00:14:45.759 --> 00:14:46.969
That's a sensitive area,

00:14:46.969 --> 00:14:48.762
given efforts in the U.S. and Europe

00:14:48.762 --> 00:14:51.473
to restrain tech transfers to China,

00:14:51.473 --> 00:14:54.184
and could damage development
if not handled carefully.

00:14:57.104 --> 00:15:00.608
As China continues to grow
and lead this industry,

00:15:00.608 --> 00:15:01.984
it will almost certainly have

00:15:01.984 --> 00:15:04.361
a bigger say in the
outcome for everyone else.

